Regression tests for SPARTA rigid-body surface objects (fix rigid)
-------------------------------------------------------------------

run_tests.py runs a set of small input decks and checks the results
against analytic expectations with tolerances:

ballistic     free body with initial velocity + angular momentum:
              straight-line COM motion, constant angular velocity
force         same body under a constant external force: COM follows
              the semi-implicit Euler trajectory to output precision
bounce        body vs static wall via push-off springs: elastic
              rebound within 1%, no tunneling into the cutoff zone
momentum      gas + body momentum conservation in a periodic box,
              within 1.5% statistical drift
overrun       body sweeping 40% of a cell per step through resting
              gas: no particles overrun (deletion counter constant)
remap         cutcell and incremental remap modes produce identical
              deterministic trajectories
multiremap    two gas-driven bodies give identical trajectories in
              cutcell and incremental modes (multi-body incremental)
staticdist    gas-driven body next to a 200-segment static circle:
              identical trajectories in both remap modes, no particles
              deleted; on several procs with --dist most static surfs
              are ghost surfs, exercising ghost-cell collisions
staticdist3d  3d: cube body drifting past a 1200-triangle static sphere,
              identical trajectories in both remap modes, no deletions;
              with --dist on several procs the sphere is mostly ghost surfs
splitcell     body sweeping alongside a diagonal wall that creates
              split cells: particles entering the swept split cells
              are reflected (no deletions), both remap modes agree
twobody       two bodies colliding head-on via push-off: symmetric,
              elastic within 2%
pushpair      ASYMMETRIC body-body contact (heavy large body vs light
              small body, corner-vs-face): total pair momentum
              conserved to output precision, verifying that contact
              forces are applied equal-and-opposite to both bodies
badmoi        negative: 3d moi violating the triangle inequality
              must be rejected
notwatertight negative: open body group must be rejected

The ballistic, force, bounce, twobody, and pushpair tests contain no
particles and must produce identical results on any number of procs.
The momentum and overrun tests are statistical and use loose
tolerances.

Usage:

  python3 run_tests.py --exe ../../../src/spa_serial
  python3 run_tests.py --exe ../../../src/spa_mpi --mpi "mpirun -np 4"
  python3 run_tests.py --exe ../../../build/src/spa_kokkos_omp --args "-k on -sf kk"

The --args string is passed to SPARTA after the executable, e.g. to
run the KOKKOS package (fix rigid/kk).  A KOKKOS build with
SPARTA_KOKKOS_EXACT reproduces the non-KOKKOS results exactly.

Passing --dist reruns the subset of tests whose decks support
distributed surfs (global surfs explicit/distributed): all but the
two negative tests.  Run it on several procs as well as on one, since
only then are static surfs stored as ghost surfs on some procs.

Exit code = number of failed tests.
